      "above_range": "Your white blood cell count is above the laboratory's reference interval, which ends at 11,500/µL. A high count most often means the body is reacting to something, usually an infection. Other common and temporary causes are hard exercise or stress shortly before the blood draw, smoking, pregnancy and medicines such as corticosteroids. Repeat the test in 2 to 4 weeks, once any infection has passed and without hard exercise that day, to confirm it. If it is still high, book an appointment with your doctor in the next few weeks. This result is not a diagnosis. Discuss it with your doctor, who knows your history. If you feel unwell, do not wait for your next appointment.",
