+   "change_vs_production": "Reference 3800-11,500/µL unchanged (Echevarne H0007). Optimal 4,500-6,000/µL → 4,100-6,000/µL (round 2; the verify file had 3,800-6,000): the floor moves to 4,100 cells/µL, where the band within 10% of the minimum hazard ratio starts in all three analyses of the Women's Health Initiative (f12-F06, f12-F07, f12-F08, f12-V01, f12-E02); 3,800 would rest on grade C evidence only (f12-E05, f12-E06, f12-E08) and a loosening needs a grade A or B quote (F12-DQ-3, PQ-f12-02). The ceiling 6,000 is kept (f12-E01, f12-V01, f12-E04, f12-E08). The below-optimal zone (3,800-4,099/µL) stays reachable, as in production, with a new message. Critical limits 2,000 and 30,000/µL added from the draft critical-limits table (critical-limits.json entries[7]). Action limit AL-14 added. Messages and note rewritten to the wording rules; in round 2 the outcome sentences that restated mortality findings were removed (confirmed ledger issue M3).",
