+   "clinical_notes_en": "The ratio of neutrophils to lymphocytes in the same blood test; the absolute counts and the percentages give the same ratio. A higher ratio can reflect inflammation in the body; it is a marker, not a treatment target, and it is read together with the two counts. It rises with age and in pregnancy and is lower on average in people of African ancestry.",
