-   "clinical_notes_en": "The ratio of neutrophils to lymphocytes in the same blood test; the absolute counts and the percentages give the same ratio. A higher ratio reflects inflammation in the body and, in large population studies, goes with poorer long-term health, but it is a marker, not a treatment target. It rises with age and in pregnancy and is lower on average in people of African ancestry.",
