enopause, hormone therapy and oral contraception: no flag (f12-E55). Coherence: a ratio can lie above its range while both counts lie inside Echevarne's wide intervals, which check K1 counts as an opposite pair (PQ-f12-07). NHANES: the programme's file has no NLR, so check N1 is not run; US adults average 2.15 (f12-E53). Round 2 (fixer, 2026-11-10): optimal floor 0.37 (F12-DQ-1): with it, neutrophils 375/µL and lymphocytes 5,330/µL (ratio 0.07) read below optimal instead of optimal; the remaining K1 pattern on this row, a ratio above the age limit with both counts inside their wide intervals, cannot be removed by a band the evidence supports (F12-DQ-2, PQ-f12-07)."
