      "above_range": "Your NLR is above the range usually seen at your age, which ends at 5.86. A high ratio means more neutrophils or fewer lymphocytes than usual and can reflect inflammation somewhere in the body. Common and temporary causes are a recent infection, hard exercise or stress shortly before the blood draw, a recent meal and medicines such as corticosteroids. Repeat the test in 2 to 4 weeks, once any infection has passed, to confirm it, and look at your neutrophil and lymphocyte counts, which have their own messages. If it is still high, discuss it with your doctor at your next check-up. This result is not a diagnosis. Discuss it with your doctor, who knows your history. If you feel unwell, do not wait for your next appointment."
